  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.2: Dropped the net8.0 build (.NET 8 is out of support; .NET 8 apps now use the netstandard2.0 build). Conversions now share one Playwright driver per process instead of starting and stopping one per conversion: faster, and avoids a Windows hang when the driver is disposed (microsoft/playwright-dotnet#3419). Fixed .NET Framework apps hanging when starting a conversion if the console code page is UTF-8 (65001), as on GitHub Actions Windows runners or servers using UTF-8 as the system code page. Fixed root-relative links (e.g. /docs/x) not being resolved against BaseUrl on Linux and macOS. Fixed FileNotFoundException for Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces when the netstandard2.0 build is used on .NET Core 3.1 / .NET 5-9. Package metadata aligned with other Rubicon Microproducts packages. 1.1.1: Documentation and package metadata for legacy .NET Framework apps (no-DI usage, calling from synchronous code, packages.config, server requirements). 1.1.0: Added net462 and netstandard2.0 targets so heavy legacy .NET Framework 4.6.2-4.8.1 apps can use the packages without upgrading their runtime; updated all dependencies.",
